// DeepSeek-V2-Lite layer 1's MLA attention over the first 1,024 keys of the latent cache (proof of
// concept): 256 tokens as two chunks of 128, head parallel (chip = head, cluster = half of a chunk's tokens: four 16-row query
// tiles), K/V tiles of 256 keys, INT8, on hemaia_16c4m_8MBL3_2cluster.
// Variant all: x multicast, the partials folded in transit (xDMA ChainGather), cross-chip dependencies in
// the BINGO hardware scheduler (per edge).
// Orders and buffers: every x multicast first, then the memory chips' pushes (x_puts_first,
// prefetch_after_x); y over the x buffers (l3_overlay); a 6-slot ring; three W slabs, K tiles in one
// and V tiles in the other two (kv_slabs split); the partial y through a half-size symmetric buffer,
// one W_O block and its ChainGather at a time (y_halves: four query tiles a cluster fit L1 only so); one
// ChainGather at a time.
// Host images: one per chiplet (per_chip_image), each holding the shared code and data and that chiplet's
// own task tables only; each cluster's L1 holds its own tasks' global ids (gid_lists), not a 2-byte entry
// for every task of the graph. The PoC twin of ../../dsv2_l1_prefill/all.
// Checks: the Q8 and the normalised O of query tiles 0 and 3 on the chip in the middle of the fold order,
// then the head and the tail of each half of y (checks stages, y_windows 4).
// What each field does is in ../../common/fa_prefill_mc.py.
{
  num_chiplets: 16
  num_clusters: 2
  model: dsv2-lite-l1
  tokens: 256
  chunk: 128
  keys: 1024
  bc: 256
  w_chunk_bytes: 147456
  w_buffers: 3
  weight_ring:
  {
    slots: 6
    batch: 4
    policy: 1
  }
  weight_crest: false
  bcast: bcast_l1
  reduce: chain
  sync: edge
  gemm_async: true
  l3_overlay: true
  x_puts_first: true
  y_halves: true
  kv_slabs: split
  y_windows: 4
  prefetch_after_x: true
  checks: stages
  chain_concurrent: false
  compact_id_maps: true
  static_l1: true
  l1_capacity: 990000
  d2d_ddr: true
  per_chip_image: true
  gid_lists: true
}
